re capitalized internally-developed software costs. Such fluctuations may not be directly proportional to changes in revenue. General and Administrative General and administrative expenses increased $1.7 million, or 7%, for the three months ended September 30, 2026 compared to the prior year period, primarily due to an increase of $1.8 million in professional fees, including legal costs. General and administrative expenses increased $8.6 million, or 12%, for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 compared to the prior year period, primarily due to increases of $6.9 million in professional fees, including legal costs, $1.2 million in software license fees, and $1.0 million in event and travel-related expenses. The increases were partially offset by a decrease of $1.0 million in refinancing expenses associated with our 2024 Term Loan B Facility (defined below) in March 2025. 35 Table of Contents General and administrative expenses may fluctuate from quarter to quarter and period to period based on the\n"}
