{"page": 54, "text": "Operating Activities Our cash flows from operating activities are primarily driven by revenue generated by our business, offset by the cash costs of operations, and are significantly influenced by the timing of and fluctuations in receipts from buyers and related payments to sellers. Our future cash flows will be diminished if we cannot increase our revenue levels and manage costs and timing of fluctuations of receipts and payments appropriately. For the nine months ended September 30, 2026, net cash provided by operating activities was $168.8 million compared to $107.7 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2025. Our operating activities included our net income of $57.8 million and non-cash adjustments of $95.5 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 and net income of $21.6 million and non-cash adjustments of $105.8 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2025. Net changes in our working capital resulted in $15.5 million of cash provided by operating activities and $19.7 million of cash used in operating activities for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025, respectively. The net changes in working capital for both periods presented were primarily due to the timing of cash receipts from buyers and the timing of payments to sellers. 41 Table of Contents Investing Activities Our primary investing activities have consisted of purchases of property and equipment, and capital expenditures in support of creating and enhancing our technology infrastructure. Purchases of property and equipment and investments in internal use software development may vary from period-to-period due to the timing of the expansion of our operations, changes to headcount, and the cycles of our internal use software development. During the nine months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025, our investing activities used net cash of $44.1 million and $63.7 million, respectively. During the nine months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025, we used cash for purchases of property and equipment of $31.4 million and $45.1 million, respectively, and used cash for investments in our internally developed software of $12.7 million and $10.1 million, respectively. During the nine months ended September 30, 2025, we also used cash of $8.1 million to acquire Streamrai, Inc. (the \"Streamr.ai Acquisition\"). Financing Activities Our financing activities consisted of repayment of amounts borrowed under our Term Loan B Facility, repayment of our Convertible Senior Notes and transactions related to our share repurchases and equity plans. For the nine months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025, net cash used in financing activities was $285.4 million and $47.0 million, respectively. Cash outflows from financing activities for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 primarily included a $205.1 million payment to settle matured Convertible Senior Notes, $55.6 million of payments related to share repurchases, $30.2 million for taxes paid related to net share\n"}
{"page": 55, "text": "settlement of stock-based awards, and $2.7 million of payments on our Term Loan B Facility. Additionally, during the nine months ended September 30, 2026, we borrowed $60.0 million under our 2024 Revolving Credit Facility to fund short-term operating requirements. The borrowings of $60.0 million were repaid during the same period, and no amounts were outstanding under the 2024 Revolving Credit Facility as of September 30, 2026. Cash outflows from financing activities for the nine months ended September 30, 2025 primarily included a $92.6 million payment to certain 2024 Term Loan B Facility lenders related to our Amendment No. 2 repricing activity, $27.3 million for taxes paid related to net share settlement of stock-based awards, and $22.9 million of payments related to share repurchases. The outflows were partially offset by cash proceeds primarily consisting of $92.6 million from certain 2024 Term Loan B Facility lenders related to our Amendment No. 2 repricing activity, cash proceeds from stock options exercises of $3.0 million, and cash proceeds from the employee stock purchase plan of $2.1 million. In connection with Amendment No. 2, $270.6 million of principal debt balance from Amendment No. 1 was rolled over as part of non-cash financing activities while the remaining $92.6 million principal balance from Amendment No. 1 was repaid and then reissued under Amendment No. 2 as mentioned above.\nContractual Obligations and Known Future Cash Requirements Our principal commitments as of September 30, 2026 consist of obligations under our 2024 Term Loan B Facility, 2024 Revolving Credit Facility, leases for our various office facilities, including our corporate headquarters in New York, New York and offices in Los Angeles, California, and operating lease agreements, including data centers and cloud hosting services that expire at various times through 2038, and the indemnification holdback associated with the Streamr.ai Acquisition. In certain cases, the terms of the lease agreements provide for rental payments on a graduated basis. 42 Table of Contents The following table summarizes our future lease obligations, payments of principal and interest under our debt agreements, and other future payments due under non-cancelable agreements at September 30, 2026 (in thousands):\nRemaining 2026 2027 2028 2029 2030 Thereafter Total\nLease liabilities associated with leases included in right-of-use lease assets as of September 30, 2026 $ 6,307 $ 22,349 $ 15,397 $ 14,798 $ 7,057 $ 2,690 $ 68,598\nObligations for leases not included in Lease Liabilities as of September 30, 2026 \u2014 \u2014 1,501 1,933 1,992 48,954 54,380\n2024 Term Loan B Facility (1) 908 3,632 3,632 3,632 3,632 342,294 357,730\nInterest, 2024 Term Loan B Facility (2) 6,511 24,870 24,684 24,362 24,108 2,427 106,962\nContractual fees related to the 2024 Term Loan B Facility and the 2024 Revolving Credit Facility (3) 153 639 639 240 38 \u2014 1,709\nIndemnification claims holdback \u2014 1,000 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 1,000\n"}
